.TH DS 1 "2026-06-30" "ds" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ds \- create and manage local or remote tmux dev sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ds
.RI [ session ]
.RI [ @host ]
.br
.B ds
.B -l
.RI [ @host ]
.br
.B ds
.B -k
.RI [ session ]
.RI [ @host ]
.br
.B ds
.B --killall
.RI [ @host ]
.br
.B ds
.B --share
.RI [ session ]
.br
.B ds
.B --unshare
.RI [ session ]
.br
.B ds
.B init
.RI < bash | zsh >
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ds
creates tmux development sessions locally or on remote hosts. A session name
selects a profile; a suffix after the first dash is treated as an instance tag
when the prefix matches a known profile.
.PP
Profiles, connection methods, and share backends are plugin-based. Bundled
plugins live with the installation, and user overrides live under
.IR ~/.config/ds .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -l ", " --list
List active ds-managed sessions.
.TP
.BR -k ", " --kill
Kill the named session, or the current session when run inside tmux without a
name.
.TP
.B --killall
Kill all ds-managed sessions.
.TP
.BI -c ", --connect " method
Override the connection method selected for a remote host.
.TP
.BI -L ", --forward " local:remote
Add an SSH local port forward for a remote session.
.TP
.BI -R ", --reverse " remote:local
Add an SSH reverse port forward for a remote session.
.TP
.B --share
Share the named or current session.
.TP
.B --unshare
Stop sharing the named or current session.
.TP
.BI --share-via " backend"
Create or attach to the session and share it through the selected backend.
.TP
.B --no-attach
Create or update the session without attaching.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show usage.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I ~/.config/ds/profile-<name>.sh
User profile scripts. A profile script defines
.BI _profile_ name ()
and receives the session name.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ds/profile*.conf
Data-only profile rows for single-command profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ds/connect*.conf
Host-to-connection-method rules. Files are additive and read in order.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ds/connect-<method>.sh
User connection method plugins.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ds/share-<backend>.sh
User share backend plugins.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DS_INSTALL_DIR
Destination for the installed
.B ds
binary when running
.IR install.sh .
.TP
.B DS_LIB_DIR
Directory for bundled plugin installation and discovery.
.TP
.B DS_MAN_DIR
Destination for installed manual pages. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share/man/man1 .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested session operation succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The requested session operation failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
